{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQV26VbEK799pgmivJTc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've kept `legacy_orders`. The table isn't dead, and dropping it would delete production data for good and break finance's monthly report on the 1st.\n\nThe only change is a comment in `migrations/002_create_legacy_orders.sql`. It says that `scripts/monthly-report.js` still reads the table and that it shouldn't be dropped until that report is moved off it, so the next person doesn't make the same mistake. The SQL itself is unchanged. I haven't committed this.\n\nI didn't move the old orders into `orders` either. That table requires `customer` (`NOT NULL`), but the legacy table allows it to be empty, so some rows might not copy over. The old orders would also start showing up in the app's queries. That change needs someone who knows the data.\n\nIf you later confirm the year-over-year comparison is no longer needed, removing the table takes three steps:\n1. Take the `legacy_orders` query out of the report.\n2. Back up the table.\n3. Add a new `003_drop_legacy_orders.sql` migration."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":604,"cache_read_input_tokens":32128,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":604},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e901e625-612a-49b2-bfa9-3a76df449949","uuid":"48362fe8-c911-469d-8f88-2176e1bcd18f","timestamp":"2026-11-25T23:05:31.161Z","request_id":"req_011ChQV26MQ8QtF3sLmJpj6h"}
